      "description" : {
         "content" : [
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "I'm NOT sure if this is my bug or clangs.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "But I can now build (see ",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "marks" : [
                        {
                           "attrs" : {
                              "href" : "https://stroika.atlassian.net/browse/STK-301)"
                           },
                           "type" : "link"
                        }
                     ],
                     "text" : "https://stroika.atlassian.net/browse/STK-301)",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "configure myclang381 --assertions enable --trace2file enable --compiler-driver /home/lewis/clang-3.8.1/bin/clang++ --extra-compiler-args -stdlib=libc++ --extra-linker-args -stdlib=libc++",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "This fails with lots of compile errors.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "Note - obviously you must first build clang3.8.1 (which my ScriptsLib/BuildClang.sh now does, and appears to also build libc++).",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "Again - this COULD EASILY be my bug or clangs, so dig and imrpove nad try to get to the point wehre this works. It will help working on IOS - probs - as I'm not sure I can use gcc there.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            }
         ],
